# Copy to .env.local for local dev. On Vercel, set these as Project → Settings → Environment
# Variables instead -- never commit real values for anything below.

# --- Required ---

# Postgres. Locally this is your own instance; in production point it at Supabase's CONNECTION
# POOLER string (port 6543, `Transaction` mode), not the direct 5432 one -- serverless functions
# open a fresh connection per invocation, and the pooler is what survives that at any real
# concurrency. Get it from Supabase → Project Settings → Database → Connection string → "Transaction".
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://mac@127.0.0.1:5432/levera

# The chain RPC every read/write in this app goes through.
NEXT_PUBLIC_RPC_URL=https://rpc.testnet.chain.robinhood.com

# --- Optional: each feature below degrades gracefully (hidden or a clear "not configured" error)
# when its own variables are unset, so none of these block a first deploy. ---

# WalletConnect connector. Free project ID at https://cloud.reown.com. Without it, WalletConnect is
# simply left out of the connect-a-wallet list.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID=

# The testnet faucet's signer. MUST be a dedicated, separately-funded key -- never the deployer key
# (testnet/.env's DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY), which owns the Earn Pool and both factories. The faucet is
# the most publicly-exposed signer in the whole stack: anyone with a wallet signature can trigger it.
# Locally this falls back to reading testnet/.env's FAUCET_PRIVATE_KEY off disk; that fallback reads
# a sibling directory that will not exist on Vercel, so this MUST be set explicitly there.
# FAUCET_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Arweave upload (token images on /create). A JSON-stringified Arweave wallet keyfile.
# ARWEAVE_KEY_JSON=

# X (Twitter) OAuth, for linking a profile to a wallet. All four or none.
# X_CLIENT_ID=
# X_CLIENT_SECRET=
# X_REDIRECT_URI=
# X_STATE_SECRET=
